  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The matrices X, A and B satisfy 2X − A = B, where A = (2 −4 / 6 0) and B = (8 2 / −2 10). (a) Determine 2X. (b) Hence determine X."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Get 2X on its own first by adding A to both sides; only then halve everything to reach X."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p200_q13.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p200-q13 from workbook page 200."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Add A to both sides to isolate 2X.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2X − A = B becomes 2X = B + A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2X = B + A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Add the matching entries of B and A.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "8 + 2 = 10; 2 + (−4) = −2; −2 + 6 = 4; 10 + 0 = 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2X = (10 −2 / 4 10)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Halve every entry of 2X.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "10 ÷ 2 = 5; −2 ÷ 2 = −1; 4 ÷ 2 = 2; 10 ÷ 2 = 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: X = (5 −1 / 2 5)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Check by substituting back.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2X − A = (10 −2 / 4 10) − (2 −4 / 6 0) = (8 2 / −2 10)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Equals B, so X is correct"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Add A to B to obtain 2X, then multiply that result by ½ to obtain X."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) 2X = B + A = (10 −2 / 4 10)  (b) X = ½(2X) = (5 −1 / 2 5)"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Matrix equations obey the same rearrangement rules as ordinary equations because addition and scalar multiplication act entry by entry. Halving a matrix means halving every element, not just the first one. Substituting the answer back reconstructs B exactly, which is a full verification."
    }
  ],
